12. Breadboard Simulation

The breadboard must behave like a real breadboard.

For example:

Power rail
────────────────────────

● ● ● ● ● ● ● ● ● ●

     IC / component

● ● ● ● ● ● ● ● ● ●

────────────────────────
Ground rail

Connections should be determined by the breadboard's actual internal
connectivity.

If two pins are inserted into electrically connected holes, the
simulator should recognize the connection.

The user should not need to manually draw abstract wires between every
logical node.

